remark: Martini 3 bead radii for HOLE (generated by tools/martini_rad.py)
remark: bead types: marrink-lab/vermouth-martinize@cfcad6ecc231 martini3001/{05-aminoacids.ff} and
remark:             marrink-lab/martini-forcefields@784591ebdc91 gmx_files/{martini_v3.0.0_ions_v1.itp,martini_v3.0.0_nucleobases_v1.itp,martini_v3.0.0_phospholipids_v1.itp,martini_v3.0.0_solvents_v1.itp}
remark: bead size:  self sigma, nonbond_params of martini_v3.0.0.itp (same commit)
remark: sources are Apache-2.0; Souza et al. (2021) Nat. Methods 18, 382
remark: covers proteins, water, ions, phospholipids and nucleobases
remark: radius = sigma/2. Residue names are the 3 characters HOLE reads.
remark: HOLE reads at most 100 VDWR lines: a bead at the regular size has no
remark: line of its own, the last line covers it.
remark: residues sharing a 3-character name (the exact name wins):
remark:   C2 CYS CYSF=2.05 CYSG=2.05 CYSP=2.35
remark:   C3 CYS CYSF=2.05 CYSG=2.05 CYSP=2.35
remark:   C4 CYS CYSF=1.7 CYSG=2.05 CYSP=2.35
remark:   SC1 CYS CYS=1.7 CYSF=1.7 CYSG=1.7 CYSP=2.35
VDWR BB   ALA 2.05
VDWR BB   GLY 2.05
VDWR BB   PRO 2.05
VDWR BB   VAL 2.05
VDWR C2   PHO 1.70
VDWR C3   PHO 2.05
VDWR C4   PHO 1.70
VDWR C5   PHO 2.05
VDWR C7   PHO 2.05
VDWR CL   ION 2.05
VDWR SC1  ALA 1.70
VDWR SC1  CYS 1.70
VDWR SC1  GLH 2.35
VDWR SC1  GLN 2.35
VDWR SC1  GLU 2.35
VDWR SC1  HID 1.70
VDWR SC1  HIE 1.70
VDWR SC1  HIP 1.70
VDWR SC1  HIS 1.70
VDWR SC1  HSD 1.70
VDWR SC1  HSE 1.70
VDWR SC1  HSP 1.70
VDWR SC1  HYP 2.35
VDWR SC1  MET 2.35
VDWR SC1  SER 1.70
VDWR SC1  TRP 1.70
VDWR SC1  TYR 1.70
VDWR SC2  ARG 2.05
VDWR SC2  LSN 2.05
VDWR SC2  LYN 2.05
VDWR SC2  LYS 2.05
VDWR SI1  EIM 2.05
VDWR BR   ??? 2.05
VDWR C1   ??? 2.05
VDWR C5   ??? 1.70
VDWR C6   ??? 1.70
VDWR C7   ??? 1.70
VDWR C8   ??? 1.70
VDWR C9   ??? 2.05
VDWR CA   ??? 2.38
VDWR CL   ??? 1.77
VDWR GL1  ??? 2.05
VDWR ID   ??? 2.05
VDWR N1   ??? 2.05
VDWR N2   ??? 1.70
VDWR N3   ??? 1.70
VDWR N4   ??? 1.70
VDWR N5   ??? 1.70
VDWR N6   ??? 1.70
VDWR NA   ??? 1.77
VDWR NO3  ??? 2.05
VDWR SC1  ??? 2.05
VDWR SC2  ??? 1.70
VDWR SC3  ??? 1.70
VDWR SC4  ??? 1.70
VDWR SC5  ??? 1.70
VDWR SCN  ??? 2.05
VDWR SI1  ??? 1.70
VDWR SI2  ??? 1.70
VDWR SI3  ??? 1.70
VDWR SI4  ??? 2.05
remark: any other bead: a regular Martini bead
VDWR ???? ??? 2.35
remark: bond radii are only read by HOLE's molqpt option
BOND ???? 1.00
